<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12125] Concurrency problem in PagesWriteThrottle</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12125</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12006&quot; title=&quot;Threads may be parked for indefinite time during throttling after spurious wakeups&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-12006&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-12006&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9231&quot; title=&quot;onMarkDirty improvement throttle implementation.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-9231&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-9231&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was added code:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
parkThrds.forEach(LockSupport::unpark);
parkThrds.clear();
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This code isn&apos;t thread-safe. We should remove from &lt;tt&gt;parkThrds&lt;/tt&gt; only unparked threads.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
